{
  "version": 1,
  "source": "hand-written: no implementation is its reference yet",
  "format": "{name, note, instructable, clients?, expect: {stub, reason?}}, as in stub-vectors.json, for a reader that takes the docs feature (Pond 1.10.0). It adds one known key, doc, on a step, a sub-step and a link, never on verify. A doc is known when it is null, or when it is exactly {\"sha256\": 64 lowercase hex, \"bytes\": a whole number from 1 to 262144} and stands beside a file (step, sub-step) or a path (link) that is present and not null. Any other doc is an unknown key at the doc itself (unknownKey:steps[0].doc, never a path inside it), so the ask is an update stub. A whole number written as a float (93.0) is not a whole number here, as the Pond reads JSON. Every other key follows stub-vectors.json. A reader without the docs feature skips this file and treats every doc as unknown. The Swift core has no unknown-key check yet, so every case carries clients [\"android\"].",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "doc-stub-step-known",
      "note": "a well-formed doc beside a step's file is known: not a stub",
      "clients": [
        "android"
      ],
      "instructable": {
        "v": 1,
        "title": "Review the release plan",
        "steps": [
          {
            "do": "Read the plan",
            "id": "s1",
            "file": "~/notes/plan.md",
            "doc": {
              "sha256": "89e032b48f654c6a542172e4396fbb6bd1cd37cfa66a5a59e987d0a3f398a4fd",
              "bytes": 93
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "stub": false
      }
    },
